      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:6:112:6",
      "text": [
        " عَلَيْكَ بِالْهِنْدَبَاءِ فَإِنَّهُ يَزِيدُ فِي الْمَاءِ وَ يُحَسِّنُ الْوَلَدَ وَ هُوَ حَارٌّ لَيِّنٌ يَزِيدُ فِي الْوَلَدِ الذُّكُورَةَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad and Ali Al Ashary, from Muhammad Bin Abdul Jabbar altogether from Al Hajjal, from Sa’alba, from a man, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘It is upon you with (eating) the endive, for it increased in the water, and improves the child birth, and it is hot, soft, increasing in the male children’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad and Abu Ali al-Ash‘ariy has narrated from Muhammad ibn ‘Abd al-Jabbar all from al-Hajj al from Tha’labah from a man who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, once said, ‘You must eat endives because it increases one’s seed and forms children well. It is hot, soft and increases male children.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
